    "body": "I completely agree that should not be revealed.\r\n\r\nDoesn't that mean though that an object's private elements should be ignored, since literally any object (i think? maybe only those with a mutable [[Prototype]]) could have private fields installed on it with the super return override trick, not just instances of classes with private fields defined?",
